  "_id": "bd-retaliation-law-of",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "(Ex. 21:23–25; Lev. 24:18–21; Deut. 19:21.) The Mosaic law aimed at making the punishment an appropriate equivalent to the offence committed. Wrongdoing must not go unpunished; on the other hand, however, the punishment must not be vindictive or excessive. In the Sermon on the Mount (Matt. 5:38–42), the Lord goes further, and urges us, so far as private wrongs to ourselves are concerned, not to retaliate at all (Rom. 12:17, 19). See also Revenge.",
